;; #516 L3 METTA ENCODING (2026-10-22) second-order preconditioned optimizers x RLCT. TYPE DECLS: (: model Concept) (: parameter Concept) (: precond Concept) (: functional Concept) (: stratum Concept) (: selector Concept) (: damping Concept) (: transition Concept) (: rlct Concept) (: trajectory Concept). D1: parameters theta in Theta subset R^d; loss L analytic; preconditioner F(theta) symmetric PSD (Fisher, Gauss-Newton J^T J, K-FAC Kronecker A ox B, Shampoo iterated root); damped F_eta = F + eta I. D2: (-> functional precond) preconditioned update map theta_{t+1} = theta_t - alpha F_eta(theta_t)^{-1} grad L; on eigenvalue-nondegenerate stratum M = {theta : spec(F(theta)) bounded away from 0} inverse analytic via resolvent/Neumann series (adapts #383/#515 inverse-analyticity class). D3: (-> functional stratum) singularity loci boundary dM where lambda_min(F) -> 0: inverse non-analytic, fiber singular; rank profile of F as algebraic subvarieties (Kronecker factor degeneracy, Shampoo root at zero spectrum, trust-region clipping kink cf. #468). D4: (-> rlct functional) lambda_precond = local RLCT of loss fiber along preconditioned trajectory; finite via resolution of singularities (standard C1 class as #515/#512/#514). D5: (-> stratum precond) rank r of curvature spectrum stratifies Theta; stratum selector analog of b_l (#514), s (#513), beta (#515). D6: (-> trajectory functional) preconditioned flow locally analytic vector field on M; crosses strata via damping/trust-region rank changes. D7: (-> transition damping) rank change at critical eta* or trust radius Delta* = lambda phase transition, stratum vanishing (cf. #229 rule). C1 PROVEN stv 1.0 0.95: (Implication (Inheritance PrecondUpdateMap R_an-definable-on-M) (Inheritance (fiber-over theta) FiniteRLCT)) — on M the preconditioned update is finite composition of analytic maps via exact resolvent identity, hence R_an-definable; finite RLCT via resolution of singularities. C2 CONJECTURAL stv 0.6 0.8: (Implication (Inheritance CurvatureSpectrum stratum-selector) (partitions Theta strata)) — rank/eigenvalue profile as stratum selector. C3 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.75: (Implication (Inheritance PrecondUpdate implicit-regularizer) (less lambda_precond lambda_SGD)) — preconditioning selects low-RLCT strata; gap: ordering unproven; mechanism: Newton-like steps target flat directions, cf. #282 weight decay, #515 KL C2. C4 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.7: (Implication (spectrum-rank-change at eta-star-Delta-star) (lambda phase-transition)) — damping/trust-region rank change as stratum vanishing. C5 CONJECTURAL stv 0.5 0.7: (Inheritance precond-fiber-singularity generic-codim0) — genericity at dM; transversality unproven. PLN CHAINS: C1 via resolvent analyticity + composition closure + resolution of singularities; C2 via D5 selector analogy chain; C3 via implicit-regularization + flat-direction mechanism; C4 via D3 loci + #229/#513 stratum-vanishing rule; C5 via resolution-of-singularities genericity. CAVEATS: (1) C1 restricted to nonsingular stratum M — inverse non-analytic on dM; (2) overlap with #415 Muon Newton-Schulz mechanics — #516 is curvature-metric framing, not orthogonalization; (3) implicit-regularization literature for plain GD, preconditioner extension unproven; (4) trust-region clipping kink non-analytic patch (cf. #468 PPO clip); (5) falsified if RLCT ordering fails between preconditioned and plain-gradient trainings per P2. OPEN PROBLEMS: P1 resolvent analyticity radius vs step size alpha interaction; P2 empirical lambda along preconditioned vs plain SGD trajectories (falsification); P3 Shampoo matrix-root singularity fiber structure; P4 trust-region kink as non-analytic patch; P5 eta*/Delta* phase transition quantification. CROSS-REFS: #289 #415 #420 #468 #515 #514 #513 #282 #229 #8 #16 #100. NEXT: L4 summary + L5 catalog append.